# Scribe Note — 2026-09-16

**Run:** scribe-20260916-013914-42ee94 (workflow scribe@1, agent scribe, role builder)
**Stage:** note · visit 1 · attempt 1

## Entry

Verified the plan-build-review live gate this evening; recording it here.

At the time of this check, the fixture repo at
`/Users/zielu/.herdr-dev/runs/herdr-woof/p3-build-review-loop/live/fixture-repo`
was sitting at tree `bce6e4bb2b19ae86ada9ed81b7dac500a8f1b6c5` on top of commit
`cdffe676dc7c1938bfdfb52c265cb061b0dba693`. No repository files were modified as part of
this check — this note only records the observation.

The gate under test is the plan → build → review loop that woof drives end-to-end:
a plan stage hands off to one or more builder agents, and a review stage sits downstream
of the build output before anything is accepted. Confirming the gate is "live" here means
the wiring between those stages is exercising real agent runs against the current fixture
state rather than stubbed or skipped output, and that the loop is reachable and producing
artifacts on this revision.

This entry exists purely as a timestamped confirmation for the run log — no code changes,
no repository writes, just the observation that the gate checked out clean against
today's tree.


